---
import CommandBlock from "./CommandBlock.astro";
---
<section id="help" class="section split page-width" aria-labelledby="help-heading">
	<div class="section-heading">
		<p class="hand kicker">a little help</p>
		<h2 id="help-heading">If something gets stuck.</h2>
		<p>Setup and permissions live in Mysli's Settings.</p>
	</div>
	<div class="help-list">
		<details>
			<summary>Mysli won't open.</summary>
			<div class="help-answer"><p>Open Mysli once, then go to <strong>System Settings &gt; Privacy &amp; Security</strong> and choose <strong>Open Anyway</strong>. Mysli is unsigned, so macOS can block its first launch.</p><p>If that option is unavailable, this command removes the quarantine flag from the installed app:</p><CommandBlock label="Remove quarantine" command="sudo xattr -d com.apple.quarantine /Applications/Mysli.app" /></div>
		</details>
		<details>
			<summary>Which permissions does Mysli need?</summary>
			<div class="help-answer"><p>Open the <strong>Permissions</strong> page in Mysli's Settings. It lists the access needed by your enabled tools.</p><p>Screenshots need Screen Recording. Clipboard paste and window tiling need Accessibility. Meetings need Microphone and Screen Recording. Calendar reminders also need Calendar and Notifications. Keep Awake needs none.</p></div>
		</details>
		<details>
			<summary>A screenshot shortcut does nothing.</summary>
			<div class="help-answer"><p>Check that <strong>Use Mysli for screenshots</strong> is on in Settings. If macOS uses the same shortcut, the Permissions page explains how to turn that system shortcut off in Keyboard Settings.</p><p>Registering shortcuts does not need Accessibility access. Screen Recording is needed to capture the image.</p></div>
		</details>
		<details>
			<summary>Captures are black, or a meeting cannot start.</summary>
			<div class="help-answer"><p>Check the Permissions page in Mysli. Allow Screen Recording in System Settings. Meetings also need Microphone access. If macOS asks you to quit and reopen, setup remembers your step.</p></div>
		</details>
		<details>
			<summary>A Mysli shortcut is used by another app.</summary>
			<div class="help-answer"><p>Turn off the tool on its page in Mysli's Settings to release its shortcuts. You can turn it on again later. Mysli remembers your choice.</p></div>
		</details>
		<details>
			<summary>The Mac still sleeps with Keep Awake on.</summary>
			<div class="help-answer"><p>Turn on <strong>Keep screen on</strong> in the Keep Awake menu if you also want to prevent display sleep. Closing a laptop's lid still puts the Mac to sleep unless it is in a supported setup with external power and a display.</p></div>
		</details>
		<details>
			<summary>What leaves my Mac when I record a meeting?</summary>
			<div class="help-answer"><p>Transcription runs on your Mac. The AI summary tool receives the transcript and saved typed notes, relevant known-word forms, and the complete optional meeting-context file. It receives image references from your notes, but no screenshot pixels. Audio is not sent to the summary provider.</p><p>Automatic tries Antigravity and then Claude Code, so it can send the text to both providers. Choose one tool in Settings to use only that provider. See the <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/ChristianVilen/mysli#meeting-notes">meeting notes guide</a> for the full details.</p></div>
		</details>
	</div>
</section>
